{"recall":{"defs":[["Support vector machine","Maximum-margin classifier."],["Support vector","Training point with α > 0 (on/inside the margin)."],["Slack variable","Amount by which a point violates its margin."],["Kernel","Inner product in a feature space computed directly."],["KKT conditions","Optimality conditions with inequality constraints."],["Hinge loss","max(0, 1 − y f(x))."]],"formulas":["M=\\frac{2}{\\|\\mathbf w\\|}","\\min\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2+C\\sum\\xi_i\\ \\text{s.t.}\\ y_i(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x_i+b)\\ge1-\\xi_i","\\max_\\alpha\\sum\\alpha_i-\\tfrac12\\sum_{i,j}\\alpha_i\\alpha_jy_iy_jK(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x_j)","f(\\mathbf x)=\\operatorname{sign}\\Big(\\sum\\alpha_iy_iK(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x)+b\\Big)","K_{RBF}=\\exp(-\\|\\mathbf x-\\mathbf z\\|^2/2\\sigma^2)"],"takeaways":["Maximum margin = minimum ½‖w‖² under y(wᵀx + b) ≥ 1.","KKT: only support vectors have α > 0; w = Σαᵢyᵢxᵢ.","Soft margin: slack, hinge loss, C trades margin vs errors.","Kernels replace dot products to give non-linear boundaries.","Multi-class via one-vs-all or one-vs-one."],"confused":[["Hard vs soft margin","No violations vs penalised slack."],["C vs γ","Violation penalty vs kernel width."],["Hinge vs log loss","Zero beyond margin vs always positive."],["OvA vs OvO","C models vs C(C − 1)/2 models."]],"minute":"An SVM finds the separating hyperplane with the largest margin. With margins at wᵀx + b = ±1, the width is 2/‖w‖, so it minimises ½‖w‖² subject to yᵢ(wᵀxᵢ + b) ≥ 1, a convex quadratic program. Lagrange multipliers and KKT give the dual, which depends only on dot products, and show that only support vectors have α > 0, with w = Σαᵢyᵢxᵢ. Soft margins add slack penalised by C via the hinge loss. Kernels such as polynomial and RBF replace dot products to give non-linear boundaries, and multiple classes use one-vs-all or one-vs-one."},"flashcards":[["Linear classifier","$f=\\operatorname{sign}(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x+b)$"],["Support vectors","Points on the margin; removing them moves the hyperplane"],["Margin width","$2/\\|\\mathbf w\\|$"],["Hard-margin primal","$\\min\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2$ s.t. $y_i(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x_i+b)\\ge1$"],["Lagrange condition","$\\nabla f=\\lambda\\nabla g$"],["KKT complementary slackness","$\\mu_j^*h_j(\\mathbf x^*)=0$"],["Dual objective","$\\sum\\alpha_i-\\tfrac12\\sum\\alpha_i\\alpha_jy_iy_j\\mathbf x_i^T\\mathbf x_j$"],["w from α","$\\mathbf w=\\sum\\alpha_iy_i\\mathbf x_i$"],["Soft margin","$\\tfrac12\\|\\mathbf w\\|^2+C\\sum\\xi_i$, $y_if\\ge1-\\xi_i$"],["Hinge loss","$\\max(0,1-yf(\\mathbf x))$"],["Large C","Small margin, fewer training errors"],["Kernel","$K(\\mathbf x_i,\\mathbf x_j)=\\phi(\\mathbf x_i)^T\\phi(\\mathbf x_j)$"],["RBF kernel","$\\exp(-\\|\\mathbf x_i-\\mathbf x_j\\|^2/2\\sigma^2)$"],["Mercer conditions","Continuous, symmetric, positive semi-definite"],["One-vs-one","$C(C-1)/2$ classifiers, majority vote"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["s-linear"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what","h2"],"deep":["s-margin"],"viz":["widestRoad"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["s-sv"],"viz":["svmPlayground"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["s-math"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["s-primal"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["s-opt"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["s-lagrange"],"viz":["lagrangeLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["s-kkt"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["s-dual"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["s-svkkt"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["s-solution"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["s-example"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8"],"deep":["s-noise"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8"],"deep":["s-slack"],"viz":["hingeLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["s-hardsoft"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":[